\label{sec:smolvla_ablation_setup}

We train an Attention-weighted Cumulative Importance Score (ACIS) module (3.46M parameters, 0.77\% of SmolVLA) to predict per-token importance scores. Training uses a Stage-1-only protocol: ACIS parameters are optimized while all VLA weights remain frozen, so that the scorer identifies important tokens under the original representation. The ablation varies three axes: \emph{scoring} (learned ACIS vs.\ random), \emph{retention ratio} $k \in \{0.50, 0.70, 0.90, 0.95\}$, and \emph{mechanism} (zero-masking, true removal, token merging via ToMe~\cite{bolya2023tome}), yielding seven configurations plus the unpruned baseline.

